.SH NAME
item_row \- See the module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ItemRow::new(title: impl Into<String>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBItemRow\fR: one row of a music, podcast, video or file list: a picture, a title with a subtitle, optional extra columns, and a trailing part (a time, a menu). Together with \fBVirtualList\fR and a \fBSortHeader\fR it is the list component.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEvery column is flex\fR (\fBFlexCells\fR). A fixed width is a *starting* size: when the row narrows, all the columns give way together, in proportion, \fBnone below what its\fR header label needs\fB, so the title is never squeezed out and a header is never cut off. The\fR header and the rows resolve the same flex, so they line up at any width.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRegular\fR: picture, then the title over its subtitle. The title column \fBgrows\fR (\fBflex\-grow: 1\fR): it covers all the width the picture, the extra columns and the suffix leave, so give the other columns fixed widths.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCompact\fR (\fBcompact\fR): no picture, and the title and subtitle share the line, each in its own column, for dense lists.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcolumn\fR adds a cell of a given width (an album, a BPM, a time); \fBsuffix\fR adds the trailing part (a menu button).
.PP
\fBThe row is content, like a \fB<tr>\fR\fR: no button, no hover, no press, no surface, and no inset unless asked for (\fBpadding\fR, or \fBinset\fR for the classic list inset). The caller wraps it in the surface that makes it a control: \fBas_button\fR: events only, so the row keeps its own layout.
.PP
.nf
.RS
ItemRow::new(&track.title)
    .subtitle(&track.artist)
    .picture(cover(track.id, 40.0))
    .column(Length::Fixed(160.0), caption(&track.album))
    .column(Length::Fixed(44.0), caption(track.time()))
    .suffix(menu_button(Icon::ViewMore, menu))
    .inset()

as_button(row).height(Length::Fill).on_press(Msg::Play(track.id))
.RE
.fi
